#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caa5349c-538c-52bc-a0cb-02fb75b868e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194112} {:answer/id #uuid "d3018d28-f0df-5bb4-8b6a-cbacb28e8eae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194113} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1b16bc-79b8-54a3-b348-ad11086c1fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194114} {:answer/id #uuid "04e8119b-4adc-5c99-b7b6-3605d597b8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194115} {:answer/id #uuid "43b1db44-48f0-57fd-acb4-24912a2f1898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caa5349c-538c-52bc-a0cb-02fb75b868e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194112} :answer-field/id #uuid "46cfab05-861f-5ef8-a1f8-fa419b795faa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3e82a60-3e6a-5448-a7f2-b8816761b999" :question/math-academy-id "q-161257" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz=$" :question/worked-solution "Since the domain of integration $R=[1,4]\\times [0,2]\\times [0,\\pi /2]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,dz & =(4-1)\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡z]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b03add-0444-56ea-a19a-ac989629bcea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365243} {:answer/id #uuid "687912df-b52a-55fb-b50e-e7f2fda30b7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365244} {:answer/id #uuid "7a7b5c7c-f132-59cd-9256-f654684f5b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365245} {:answer/id #uuid "44baa4c6-de18-5146-8462-6ae1b0b37e0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365246} {:answer/id #uuid "0847be0a-2ecf-5d2c-b9be-b5fab51f00d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b03add-0444-56ea-a19a-ac989629bcea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365243} :answer-field/id #uuid "d35092d7-e125-5886-bea0-e211c6d92196" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "283cdf8c-c107-502f-8e66-6810691011a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161269" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "Since the domain of integration $R=[0,4]\\times [1,2]\\times [0,1]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,dx{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,dx{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,dz & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(8-0)\\cdot (\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1bbd036-3307-5246-9074-b7523ccdafa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365250} {:answer/id #uuid "94b37b6e-e045-54ba-ac63-494c3e3681c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365251} {:answer/id #uuid "e9bf9218-4d15-54b2-b615-9878dff577b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365252} {:answer/id #uuid "b97719b3-ee77-57f6-bc51-3ed63de4b6f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365253} {:answer/id #uuid "2342a0ce-bde6-5973-9225-be71278631ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2342a0ce-bde6-5973-9225-be71278631ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365254} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c842a99-4831-51a6-bb06-5707b68011df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6873c098-2f5d-5723-abba-bfc2f14a77ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-161295" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{e}{e}^{-z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "Since the domain of integration $R=[0,2]\\times [0,e]\\times [0,1]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{e}{e}^{-z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}dx{\\int }_{0}^{e}dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-z}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}dx{\\int }_{0}^{e}dy{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-z}\\,dz & =(2-0)\\cdot (e-0)\\cdot [-{e}^{-z}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot e\\cdot (-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2e(1-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2e-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c17ff49b-2d33-583b-b115-6f65d8ab4f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(e - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194118} {:answer/id #uuid "f48a7830-50c8-56c3-93e7-568e07944915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194119} {:answer/id #uuid "1da13f3c-d1f9-56c8-b514-2e8bc8b651e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194120} {:answer/id #uuid "277f3f55-39b4-5b83-9482-8f1b6b9f65e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(e^{2} - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194121} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec3eb80-940f-5dfa-ad3b-ab9801fe7095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec3eb80-940f-5dfa-ad3b-ab9801fe7095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194122} :answer-field/id #uuid "94665de8-bffc-5087-85a9-85db88a7b775" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6c96e1a-8e86-57e2-bade-8a9c9d51ce96" :question/math-academy-id "q-161345" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{z+1}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{z+1}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{z+1}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}2[{e}^{z+1}]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}2({e}^{x+1}-e)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}2({e}^{x+1}-e)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[2{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{e}^{x+1}-e\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2[{e}^{x+1}-ex]_{x=-y}^{x=0}\\,dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{0+1}-e(0)-({e}^{-y+1}-e(-y))dy \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}e-{e}^{1-y}-ey\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{0}^{1}e-{e}^{1-y}-ey\\,dy & =2{[ey+{e}^{1-y}-\\frac{e}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =2(e(1-0)+{e}^{1-1}-{e}^{1-0}-\\frac{e}{2}({1}^{2}-{0}^{2})) \\\\  & =2(e+1-e-\\frac{e}{2}) \\\\  & =2-e\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "413e69f8-af3f-5c03-9e44-2b7a19d51104" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365257} {:answer/id #uuid "00b2c4eb-53d0-535c-8782-556240454213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365258} {:answer/id #uuid "c42a15ad-87f3-52fd-9a2b-140dfaf1bac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365259} {:answer/id #uuid "9a483e68-03a4-5858-998e-8bc7a8f254d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365260} {:answer/id #uuid "80c6febf-8958-5563-b7ac-7d8ee11fec98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c42a15ad-87f3-52fd-9a2b-140dfaf1bac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365259} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1623a82-4242-52bf-96f1-a066ea237813" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9afcd968-6275-532c-b4e4-869d34d53716" :question/math-academy-id "q-162536" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{y}xyz\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{y}xyz\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}xyz\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{[\\frac{1}{2}xy{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}xy({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{3}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{3}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{3}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{8}x{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{8}x({x}^{4}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}(64-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
